---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import routeMap from '../assets/images/route-map-desktop.jpg';
---

<section class="route-intro section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="route-intro__copy reveal">
      <h1>The Route</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        There are sixteen historical cannons to link up in order. If riding the route, you'll need
        to choose your bike carefully as there is a mixture of terrain, including road, cobbles,
        gravel and even some single-track. The majority of the route is paved, but just as it
        starts getting tough towards the end of the route, you'll hit the gravel (and some
        single-track) and start to make your way on the trails around the mountain before dropping
        back down to your starting point at East City Cycles.
      </p>
      <div class="route-intro__ctas">
        <a href="https://www.komoot.com/tour/1000368153" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn">
          View on Komoot
        </a>
        <a href="/cape-town-cannon-challenge.gpx" download class="btn btn--outline-light">
          Download GPX
        </a>
      </div>
      <p class="route-intro__stats">16 cannons &ndash; 160km &ndash; 2750m elevation</p>
    </div>

    <Image
      src={routeMap}
      alt="Map of the Cape Town Cannon Challenge route around the Cape Peninsula"
      width={1600}
      height={1200}
      loading="lazy"
      class="route-intro__map reveal"
    />
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .route-intro {
    background: #000;
    color: #fff;
  }

  .route-intro h1 {
    color: #fff;
  }

  .route-intro__copy {
    max-width: 60rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
    margin-bottom: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.5rem);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .route-intro__copy .lede {
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9);
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .route-intro__ctas {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .route-intro__stats {
    font-family: var(--font-title);
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #fff;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    max-width: none;
  }

  .route-intro :global(.route-intro__map) {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }
</style>
